            {
                "entry_id": "6c424ff7-c264-3b6e-9b19-abb6b30e87b3",
                "word": "phlébotomie",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "95af00e8-5d1a-48f4-853f-99cdd8a31356",
                        "entry_id": "6c424ff7-c264-3b6e-9b19-abb6b30e87b3",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "phlébotomies"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a3797a28-a093-37b3-9287-56508fbaf1d0",
                        "entry_id": "6c424ff7-c264-3b6e-9b19-abb6b30e87b3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Saignée, art de saigner."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "dated"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9bbf57ca-ae89-411e-a8e8-926878e8632e",
                                "sense_id": "a3797a28-a093-37b3-9287-56508fbaf1d0",
                                "text": "Je voudrais qu'on saignât les prêtres une fois par mois. Oui, madame Lefrançois, tous les mois, une large phlébotomie, dans l'intérêt de la police et des mœurs !"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ee319533-a7e6-3f64-b967-7b8e8df2e10a",
                        "entry_id": "6c424ff7-c264-3b6e-9b19-abb6b30e87b3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Prélèvement sanguin, prise de sang."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Hématologie"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b1c30bb3-4da2-4986-99c2-a8c36004238b",
                        "source_entry_id": "6c424ff7-c264-3b6e-9b19-abb6b30e87b3",
                        "target_lang_word": "Aderlass",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Aderlass",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "03287503-81d8-3783-aa4b-4bc57f7bc6b6",
                                        "entry_id": "107d2bf0-86ea-3ad1-848b-8af481a0f047",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Absaugenlassen von Blut durch Blutegel, früher auch Ablaufenlassen von Blut"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e8a723c6-42fb-40a0-a12d-74fd224a38de",
                                                "sense_id": "03287503-81d8-3783-aa4b-4bc57f7bc6b6",
                                                "text": "Der König wurde durch allzu häufigen Aderlass derart geschwächt, dass er seinen Krankheiten erlag."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "83c482b6-9eb6-4ad7-a135-3ec91c87f012",
                                                "sense_id": "03287503-81d8-3783-aa4b-4bc57f7bc6b6",
                                                "text": "„Da er keine andere Behandlungsmethode kannte, fuhr er mit dem Aderlass fort und verabreichte Einläufe, die den Körper purgieren sollten.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5f8bb73e-aedb-4f62-bd60-12a50523d717",
                                                "sense_id": "03287503-81d8-3783-aa4b-4bc57f7bc6b6",
                                                "text": "„Der Regimentsarzt kam und fand einen Aderlass notwendig.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "343fd925-c085-323c-9ec5-da767f4a3928",
                                        "entry_id": "107d2bf0-86ea-3ad1-848b-8af481a0f047",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "bedeutender Substanzverlust"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figurative"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b1bdd263-e70b-4026-8824-603561f32819",
                                                "sense_id": "343fd925-c085-323c-9ec5-da767f4a3928",
                                                "text": "Mathematik und Naturwissenschaft an deutschen Hochschulen haben den Aderlass durch Vertreibung der jüdischen Forscher ab 1933 niemals überwunden, und damit verlor die deutsche Sprache auch ihren Weltrang in diesen Fächern."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b224c6e7-8a39-4331-9070-09580c8f2abb",
                                                "sense_id": "343fd925-c085-323c-9ec5-da767f4a3928",
                                                "text": "„Indessen ging der Vormarsch der Roten Armee nicht so glatt wie erwartet, und der Preis für das Vorankommen war hoch, der Aderlass gewaltig.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1d025504-8667-44db-b856-7e9fd3d56cda",
                        "source_entry_id": "6c424ff7-c264-3b6e-9b19-abb6b30e87b3",
                        "target_lang_word": "phlebotomy",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "phlebotomy",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f0cc605a-138f-312b-859a-bb93a1c094bd",
                                        "entry_id": "b470655d-b9a6-311d-ae69-94d1e3bd4ff4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The opening of a vein, either to withdraw blood or for letting blood; venesection."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "be150b70-1065-4e99-9773-0fe8a7aba29e",
                                                "sense_id": "f0cc605a-138f-312b-859a-bb93a1c094bd",
                                                "text": "Now butter with a leafe of Sage is good to Parge the bloud, Fly Venus and Phlebotomy for they are neither good."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "883908b0-2347-48f4-b419-3920557a526e",
                                                "sense_id": "f0cc605a-138f-312b-859a-bb93a1c094bd",
                                                "text": "Phlebotomy is promiscuously used before and after physick, commonly before and upon occasion is often reiterated, if there be any need at least of it."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bd48cdf8-9157-479f-990e-0482602d9846",
                                                "sense_id": "f0cc605a-138f-312b-859a-bb93a1c094bd",
                                                "text": "He had even taken from his pocket a cupping apparatus, and was about to proceed to phlebotomy, when the object of his anxious solicitude suddenly revived […]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ec84433f-c3d3-4803-b1c9-c0187a3f6a24",
                                                "sense_id": "f0cc605a-138f-312b-859a-bb93a1c094bd",
                                                "text": "Of course, members of the family were foremost in spilling loyal blood on Marston Moor, that great field of plebotomy to so may Cavaliers."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "340002a6-0c29-4694-bc36-1c0b31720c62",
                                                "sense_id": "f0cc605a-138f-312b-859a-bb93a1c094bd",
                                                "text": "Then she made an impatient gesture with her hand. \"Time was, my dear colleague, when a snuff-box was as much part of my equipment as my phlebotomy case.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
